## 7. Promotion Tracking — Lazy Load

Russell is tracking promotion readiness (Senior GP3 → Staff GP4 / Lead MG1). Working
files live at `~/Documents/promotion/`.

**Load `~/Documents/promotion/CLAUDE.md` when ANY of these fire:**

- User explicitly mentions promo / promotion / Staff / Lead / Manager / review cycle / 1:1 prep / brag doc.
- User asks "what's my promo status", "ready for Staff", "log this for promotion", "where do I stand".
- User says "log this" / "track this" in context of work that just happened.
- Activity signals appear in conversation, EVEN UNPROMPTED — proactively offer to log:
  - Design doc written, architecture decision made, cross-team API contract changed (criterion 2/3).
  - Mentoring moment, onboarded a peer, taught via code review (criterion 6).
  - Tech debt identified/paid down proactively (criterion 5).
  - Tool/tech/process evaluated or introduced (criterion 4).
  - Owned an epic end-to-end (criterion 1).
  - Coordinated daily team activity, gave teammate feedback, covered lead duties (mgmt).

On load, follow the routing in that file (criteria 1–6 → `se-log.md`, mgmt → `mgmt-log.md`).
For right-leveling questions, also load `~/Documents/promotion/reference/se-track.md` and/or
`sem-track.md` (all-levels detail).

Do NOT load these files for unrelated work — silent background otherwise.
